From: nura-builds
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/mdss: an optional misc_ahb clock for MDP5

On MSM8226 the MDSS registers need MMSS_MISC_AHB_CLK, which only the DSI
controller enabled ("core_mmss"): after a blank (the DSI powered down) the
MDP's registers were unreachable and unblanking crashed with external
aborts (mdp5_crtc_atomic_flush, mdp5_ctl_set_cursor), even the MDP's
version register faulted with the MDP runtime-active. Take an optional
"misc_ahb" clock in the MDSS node, enabled with the others while the MDSS
is active.
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_mdss.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_mdss.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_mdss.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_mdss.c
@@ -409,7 +409,7 @@
 /*
  * MDP5 MDSS uses at most three specified clocks.
  */
-#define MDP5_MDSS_NUM_CLOCKS 3
+#define MDP5_MDSS_NUM_CLOCKS 4
 static int mdp5_mdss_parse_clock(struct platform_device *pdev, struct clk_bulk_data **clocks)
 {
 	struct clk_bulk_data *bulk;
@@ -426,6 +426,11 @@
 	bulk[num_clocks++].id = "iface";
 	bulk[num_clocks++].id = "bus";
 	bulk[num_clocks++].id = "vsync";
+	/*
+	 * MSM8226: MMSS_MISC_AHB_CLK, else only the DSI's: register access to the MDSS fails when
+	 * the DSI powers down while the MDP is still in use (optional)
+	 */
+	bulk[num_clocks++].id = "misc_ahb";
 
 	ret = devm_clk_bulk_get_optional(&pdev->dev, num_clocks, bulk);
 	if (ret)
